472
00:41:16,140 --> 00:41:18,720
The flames quickly spread to a truck

473
00:41:18,721 --> 00:41:21,720
loaded with 20 tons of animal fat.

474
00:41:22,080 --> 00:41:29,600
The resulting inferno reached a temperature of 1300 degrees and had passengers gasping on the train car floor.

475
00:41:30,900 --> 00:41:35,680
The shuttle tried to race through to the British side so that firemen could work in the open air,

476
00:41:35,681 --> 00:41:43,160
but wind generated by the speeding train spread the fire from wagon to wagon until 14 of the 28 cars were ablaze.

477
00:41:43,720 --> 00:41:47,700
Finally, the Euro shuttle came to a stop about 10 miles out of Calais.

478
00:41:47,701 --> 00:41:50,700
By the time it was halted in the middle of the tunnel,

479
00:41:50,701 --> 00:41:54,700
most of the train was a raging inferno.

480
00:41:54,701 --> 00:41:57,700
And all the wagons were melted down,

481
00:41:57,701 --> 00:41:59,700
just like huge dollops of metal.

482
00:41:59,701 --> 00:42:02,700
And they did have to be prized away from the line.

483
00:42:02,701 --> 00:42:04,700
The line was totally destroyed.

484
00:42:04,701 --> 00:42:06,700
And it was very, very lucky that nobody was killed.

485
00:42:06,701 --> 00:42:09,700
That's because they managed to get out of the train

486
00:42:09,701 --> 00:42:12,700
and into the service tunnel and away from the danger.

487
00:42:12,701 --> 00:42:19,540
from a danger the fire then began to eat into the into the main superstructure of the tunnel

488
00:42:19,541 --> 00:42:25,760
itself given another hour or two if that fire hadn't been brought under control maybe they

489
00:42:25,761 --> 00:42:30,760
would have been a collapse which would have brought the whole thing down as a result of

490
00:42:30,761 --> 00:42:37,600
the near catastrophe Euro tunnel has made key changes in its firefighting strategy instead

491
00:42:37,601 --> 00:42:42,680
of ramming through to daylight in a literal blaze, the plan now is to stop in the tunnel,

492
00:42:42,980 --> 00:42:48,740
let passengers escape to safety, and fight the fire with hoses and suppressants on board the

493
00:42:48,741 --> 00:42:54,982
train. The fire has certainly not deterred people from using the channel.

494
00:42:54,983 --> 00:42:57,120
31 million people a year,

495
00:42:57,121 --> 00:43:02,712
a thousand cars an hour, now cross the English Channel from below.

496
00:43:02,713 --> 00:43:05,000
Many of them make day trips

497
